@page "/docs/data-views"

<Page>
    <DocsExample Title="DataView" ComponentType="typeof(DataView<>)">
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsBasic)" Title="Local items">
            <Description>
                Bind a list with <code>Items</code> and describe the data with <code>DataColumn</code>s.
                Search matches word by word across the searchable columns: <code>ada 2026</code> finds rows
                where "ada" is in one column and "2026" in another. Quotes keep a phrase together.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsList)" Title="List view">
            <Description>
                The same engine can show items as a list. <code>Views</code> adds a view switcher to the toolbar;
                switching keeps the page, sort and search. Views without column headers get a sort menu.
                <code>DataListItem</code> gives the common layout: avatar, title, subtitle and meta. Without a
                <code>ListItemTemplate</code>, the columns build "Label: value" lines.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsRemote)" Title="Remote data with ItemsProvider">
            <Description>
                <code>ItemsProvider</code> receives a <code>DataRequest</code> (paging, sorts, search terms, filters and
                the columns' member paths) and returns a <code>DataPage</code>. The view waits for a typing pause before
                searching, cancels the previous request and ignores late responses. The request serializes to JSON, so it
                can be posted to an API; the server must check every column and operator against an allow-list.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsFilters)" Title="Column filters">
            <Description>
                <code>Filterable</code> picks a control from the value type: text, a from–to range for numbers and dates,
                checkboxes for enums, Yes/No for bools, and "empty" for nullable values. <code>FilterOperators</code> adds an
                operator picker. Filters reach sources as <code>FilterSpec</code>s by column id; <code>@@bind-Filters</code>
                saves or restores them, and <code>ShowFilterChips</code> lists the active ones.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsCursor)" Title="Cursor paging">
            <Description>
                A source with <code>PagingMode.Cursor</code> and no total count gets next and previous buttons only.
                The view remembers the cursor of each visited page.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsVirtualize)" Title="Virtualization">
            <Description>
                <code>Virtualize</code> shows one scrolling list and renders only the visible rows. Offset sources with a total
                fetch the visible range; cursor sources (or sources without a total) load the next page as you near the end.
                Rows need a fixed height (<code>ItemSize</code>) and the view a <code>Height</code>.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsCalculated)" Title="Calculated columns">
            <Description>
                <code>Value</code> takes any expression. The members it uses are found automatically, so sort and search
                work on calculated values. <code>SortBy</code> and <code>FilterBy</code> use other properties instead.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsStyling)" Title="Row links and styling">
            <Description>
                <code>RowHref</code> makes each row a real link (Ctrl-click opens a new tab). Rows and cells can be
                colored from their data with Tabler colors, which follow the theme. Pair color with text for accessibility.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsEditing)" Title="Editing">
            <Description>
                A <code>SaveItem</code> handler turns editing on. Rows are edited on a copy (the draft), so Cancel just throws
                it away and the real row changes only when the handler returns <code>EditResult.Saved</code>. Return
                <code>EditResult.Failed(message)</code> or <code>EditResult.Invalid((field, message))</code> to keep the draft
                and show the problem. Inline, popup and drawer editing share the same flow; Enter saves and Esc cancels.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsRowActions)" Title="Row actions">
            <Description>
                Declared actions render the same way everywhere: icon buttons for the first few, then a menu. Actions can be
                links, show a spinner while their handler runs, ask for confirmation and depend on the row.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsSelection)" Title="Selection and bulk actions">
            <Description>
                Selection is tracked by key, so it survives paging, searching and reloads. With rows selected, the header becomes
                a selection bar with the bulk actions. "Select all matching" hands the current request to the action instead of
                every row, so a server can act on all of them.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsDetails)" Title="Details">
            <Description>
                Details are separate from selection and can show inline, in a drawer or in a side panel beside a list.
                <code>LoadDetails</code> loads extra data when details open, cached per item.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
        <CodeSnippet SetBackground Component="@typeof(DataViewsState)" Title="State">
            <Description>
                <code>@@bind-State</code> exposes paging, sort, search and filters as a serializable
                <code>DataViewState</code>, to save, restore or drive the view.
            </Description>
        </CodeSnippet>
    </DocsExample>
</Page>
